WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:08.071
If your operator digs through a box of mixed parts, you are paying for every second of that search.

00:00:08.671 --> 00:00:13.713
Loose parts in deep boxes slow assembly and lead to the wrong part being fitted.

00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:17.270
Small fasteners and connectors are the worst offenders.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:23.633
A bin rail holds plastic bins in a row, each with one part, at the height the operator needs.

00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:28.395
Mounted flat, or tilted at 15 degrees, the bins face the operator,

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.721
so each part can be seen and picked in one reach.

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:34.412
Arrange the bins in the order of assembly.

00:00:34.692 --> 00:00:39.562
Label each bin clearly, and refill from behind, so the line never runs dry.

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:46.486
One gas-detector maker's Scitec stations each carry a six-bin rail for fasteners and connectors,

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:48.529
right above the soldering area.

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:54.415
On Flexi, heavy-duty parts bin rails and utility bins mount in the micro slots.

00:00:55.015 --> 00:00:57.859
Present parts in sequence and assembly speeds up.

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:00.146
How do your operators pick parts today?

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:04.579
Comment below, and next, see how variable-angle shelves save backs.

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:09.424
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

